## DETAILED WEAKNESSES & REQUIRED REVISIONS

### Critical Revisions (Must Fix Before Journal Submission)

1. **Dataset Scale-Up ($N \ge 500$)**:
   - *Requirement*: Execute the evaluation pipeline on the 500-document benchmark dataset (`synthetic-dataset-500`) to compute confidence intervals, standard deviations, and statistical significance ($p$-values via Wilcoxon signed-rank test).

2. **Reference Metadata Cleanup**:
   - *Requirement*: Remove all `[NEEDS VERIFICATION]` placeholders from References [5], [6], [7], [13], [17], [24], [25] and fix malformed author strings in Ref [31].

3. **Pre-HITL vs. Post-HITL Metric Disaggregation**:
   - *Requirement*: Explicitly report raw AI extraction F1 ($F1_{raw}$) separately from post-HITL verified F1 ($F1_{final}$) in Table 6 to clearly isolate the AI model performance from human correction contribution.

### Optional Improvements (Nice to Have)

1. **Cloud Document AI Baseline Addition**: Include AWS Textract or Google Cloud Document AI as an additional baseline in Table 1 and Section 6.
2. **Cost Analysis Breakdown**: Include an API cost column (\$/1,000 documents) in Table 6 comparing Gemini 2.5 Flash vs. OpenRouter gpt-4o-mini vs. Tesseract.

